\begin{description}
\item[* name:] FPrepppropOverIO
\item[* relevant examples:] 
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule (filter)
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] TC:XPoverIO  (* ?? *)
\item[* date of creation:] 21-JUN-1988 15:30:00  
\item[* author:] Elly van Munster
\item[* copied from:] TPrepppropOverIO
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] 
To block structures where the transformation PrepppropOverIO
didn't apply (i.e. the transformation should apply if possible).
The (negative!) filter works as follows:\\
The input model of the filter is identical to the input model
of the transformation. Now, the Transformation is optional, BUT:\\
- If it doesn't apply (while it could), the filter blocks the model.\\
- If it does apply, the model is no correct input for the filter anymore.
